[2026-09-18 14:33:47] REQ 260918143159-12 RESPONSE http=200 body_tail={"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-18T14:33:47.618655988Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":"","tool_calls":[{"id":"call_3z3qtv3a","function":{"index":0,"name":"execute_code_local","arguments":{"command":"cat \u003e /tmp/gh_comment.md \u003c\u003c'EOF'\n**Update 2026-09-18 -- both mechanisms confirmed live on master, zero reconnects since the issue was posted, and a wedge-class failure mode**\n\nPosting a follow-up after a day of continued observation, all against the same 7-camera frigate 0.17.2 system (go2rtc 1.9.10).\n\n**1. Zero reconnects in ~19h with the page closed.**\n\n`go2rtc` logs show 0 reconnect lines since this issue was filed (2026-09-17T19:43Z). For comparison, the 3 live-page loads on 09-16 produced 3 fleet-wide reconnect waves (7 sessions remade in the same second, frigate watchdogs restarted all ffmpeg processes ~20-24s later). The trigger really is the live page's per-camera metadata probe (`microphone=` param) and nothing else on our system.\n\n**2. The AddTrack path is still undeduped on master.**\n\nRe-checked `pkg/rtsp/consumer.go` on master today: `Conn.AddTrack` in the ModeActiveProducer branch still hits `if c.state == StatePlay { c.Reconnect() }` unconditionally, with no check against existing `c.Senders`. Also re-verified that commit fde1fdc5 (recent rtsp refactor) touched `consumer.go` but did not touch this path -- the asymmetry with `Conn.GetTrack`'s pointer-equality receiver dedup (`pkg/rtsp/producer.go`) is unchanged.\n\n**3. New: the blast radius is worse than a 20s stall -- consumers can wedge.**\n\nA single-probe reproducer (one `GET /api/streams?src=\u003ccam\u003e\u0026video=all\u0026audio=all\u0026microphone=`, no page load) remade the producer's RTSP session as expected. But on the remade session the downstream frigate recorder did not just stall -- it entered a restart loop for ~3 minutes (`No frames received in 20 seconds` x3+, ending in `vf#1 Function not implemented -\u003e Nothing was written`) and never self-healed. It took a go2rtc stream reload (DELETE+PUT on `/api/streams?src=\u003ccam\u003e`) to recover. So on some consumer/codec combinations the probe doesn't cost 20s of downtime, it costs a manual intervention. This strengthens the case for direction (a) -- dedup in `Conn.AddTrack` against existing senders -- since the probe buys the requester nothing (the metadata response is identical without the reconnect).\n\nHappy to test a patch or provide more logs (full producer remake timeline, ffmpeg restart-loop logs) if useful.\nEOF\nwc -c /tmp/gh_comment.md"}}}]},"done":false}\n{"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-18T14:33:47.619454178Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":""},"done":false}\n{"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-18T14:33:47.689908775Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":""},"done":true,"done_reason":"stop","total_duration":2876274688,"prompt_eval_count":23667,"prompt_eval_cached_count":17920,"eval_count":588}\n(fd3e58e68cdf2d60df604afa4bf00f49 . 649)
