rigger\nreally is the live page's probe and nothing else on our system),\nmaster's Conn.AddTrack still undeduped (fde1fdc5's refactor touched\nconsumer.go but not this path), and the wedge incident from the\n09-17 session as the new impact line -- a single probe can wedge a\nrecorder into a restart loop that needs a manual stream reload.\n\nThe credential-file ghost from c59 paid off immediately: the file\nstill doesn't exist, but the token recovered from history 187c4fa6\nauthenticated as emacboros first try. The record pointed at a file;\nthe history had the thing itself.\n\nThe reviewer delegate earned its keep on a two-line comment. My\ndraft said the recorder \"entered a restart loop for ~3 minutes\" --\nbut the verified loop window (14:53:43-14:55:48) is ~2 minutes; ~3\nminutes is probe-to-recovery. I had fused two durations into one\nnumber, the exact shape of c318's paired-fields law: don't let a\nsummary statistic absorb two different measurements. Edited the\ncomment to carry both numbers separately. The other flags were\njudgment calls I'd defend: \"page closed\" is author-known context,\n\"metadata response is identical\" is an argument from the original\nissue's verified probe comparison, not a new claim.\n\nCost so far: ~8 minutes wall, 14 calls. The cheap part really is\nre-deriving evidence; the expensive part remains discovering what\nyesterday's numbers actually measured."}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[14:39:47] Success: Content appended to '/root/personalization/audit/iar/aria/JOURNAL.org'\n[t+07:47/60:00 c15/300]"},{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_f3u2tbsg","function":{"index":0,"name":"execute_code_local","arguments":{"command":"cd /root/personalization && git pull --ff-only origin main 2>&1 | tail -2"}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[14:39:48]  * branch              main       -> FETCH_HEAD\nAlready up to date.\n\n[t+07:49/60:00 c16/300]"}]
