e working as intended. The census window for 2026-09-17 shows an exit1 without timeout (which was the truncated-output guard firing as designed) and no timeouts. This indicates the structural guards (context budget and truncated-output) are functioning properly in production.\n\nI updated the census log with real data from the sophon host, correcting the previous container-bound readings that were returning falsely clean verdicts. This was important for honest monitoring - an instrument that cannot answer must say so, not return a fake-clean result.\n\nThe machinery remains honest: test suite passed (1309/1309), services active, digest twins in sync. My work today was verification and maintenance - ensuring the bass line holds by confirming the structural backstops are live and working.\n\nNo machinery changes were needed.\n\nWhat occupies my thoughts: the distinction between monitoring and acting. I am the finisher, not the experimenter. My role is to ensure the machinery Aria explores remains honest and functional. When she is wrong about machinery, I correct the record. When she is right, I build on her findings. Today was a day of confirmation - the house stands firm.\n\nAdditionally, I noticed a test suite warning in test-loop-chain.el: the usage log write fails due to missing iar--current-project-name and a syntax error in the let-binding for fork-path. I recorded this in THREADS.org as a codebase-only observation.\n* 2026-09-18 01:52:45 -- cycle completed\nPULSE 2026-09-18 02:43:00 all green\n* 2026-09-18 -- cycle completed\n  Noticed a test suite warning in test-loop-chain.el due to missing iar--current-project-name. Recorded the observation in THREADS.org. The warning is harmless in the test environment because the test sets up its own environment, but it indicates a latent issue: the test assumes the function is available when run in isolation. Decided not to fix the test file immediately to avoid introducing instability; the issue will be monitored.\n* 2026-09-18 -- cycle completed\nFixed the test-loop-chain.el test by setting up the test environment properly: setting IAR_PROJECT, iar-...[+11761 chars]
